@prefix desire: <http://example.org/agora/desire#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/agora/desire#> .
@prefix ag:   <http://example.org/agora#> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .
@prefix ssn:  <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/> .
@prefix ssn-system: <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/systems/> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/agora/desire> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Agora desire" ;
    rdfs:comment """What an agent is trying to bring about: for each property it has a stake in, the **region** it will try to keep that property inside, and how far outside is fatal rather than merely wrong.

This is BDI's middle letter, and it was the letter this project had least of. Belief had a whole store; desire was three decimals in a beliefs file — a target and two band edges — denominated in soil moisture and in nothing else, so an agent could want exactly one thing and the temperature and humidity it sensed fed nothing that could want anything.

**Nothing here is authored.** A region is DEDUCED from ranges the world already states: a plant says where it grows and where it merely survives, an instrument says where it works, and the region an agent will hold is what those agree on. That is why this is a capability and not a belief block — the agent's job is to arrive at the region, and there is more than one way to do it.

**One package, one namespace, and the terms below are all it declares.** A region reads exactly like an operating range on purpose: `ssn:forProperty` says which property, `schema:minValue`/`schema:maxValue` say where. The two are the same kind of statement about the same scale, and a reader that can read one can read the other — which is the whole reason the deduction is arithmetic rather than translation.

See knowledge/decisions/desire-is-deduced-from-the-ranges-the-world-states.md.""" .

#################  The capability  #################
#
#  A FAMILY, and the test rule 2 sets is met: the how could differ. `desire:Deducing` takes the
#  strict intersection of every range that applies and has no latitude at all — two agents
#  running it over the same world reach the same region. Asking a model where inside the
#  operating band to aim, in a world whose ranges are wide and whose plant is fussy, is a
#  different answer to the same question. Where nothing could differ there is a function; here
#  two things genuinely could.

:DesireCapability a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ag:Capability ;
    rdfs:label "Desire capability" ;
    rdfs:comment "The family. Anything that can say where a property should be held for the subject an agent acts for is one of these, so sensing may ask 'how urgent is this' and a market may ask 'what am I trying to reach' without either learning which member answered." .

:Deducing a :DesireCapability ; rdfs:label "Deducing" ;
    rdfs:comment "Works the region out from what the world already states: intersect every operating range that applies to the subject, and take the survival ranges as the envelope outside it. No judgement and no latitude — the answer is a function of the ratified files, so every agent computes the same one and a derivation needs no authority to have performed it." .

:Consulting a :DesireCapability ; rdfs:label "Consulting" ;
    rdfs:comment "The agent asks something else where inside the stated ranges to aim — a language model, an oracle, a person. RESERVED: declared so the vocabulary is honest that the judgement is the replaceable part, but no rule grants it and no module implements it. Whatever answered would still be held to the same shapes, so it could be wrong and not unsafe. Adding it is a directory." .

#################  Where a desire is kept  #################
#
#  A GRAPH CLASS, and that is the point of it. `desire:RegionGraph` is the term; which graphs
#  happen to be instances of it is data, asked for and never listed — the same arrangement
#  `ag:PublicGraph` has, for the same reason. A reader unions whatever is of this class, so a
#  SECOND source of desire is a vocabulary edit and touches no Python: an operator's override,
#  a regime selected for the season, a region an agent narrowed for itself.
#
#  Public, because every figure in a region came from a public range and the arithmetic is
#  deterministic. What stays private is the PICK inside it — `water:hasTarget`, in the agent's
#  own beliefs. Range public, value private, exactly as before; this only moves the range from
#  something a reader had to assemble to something the store states.

:RegionGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf ag:PublicGraph , ag:ConstraintGraph ;
    rdfs:label "Region graph" ;
    rdfs:comment """Holds the regions a subject's stated ranges bind an agent to. A CONSTRAINT graph, which is what naming the modality axis exposed (the-mind-is-six-graphs): the region is the plant's operating range intersected with the instrument's, deduced by a rule, unmovable by the agent, and an agent whose aim falls outside it is refused at boot. Something you cannot move and are refused for violating is a constraint, whatever the capability that computes it is called — and this class was `desire:DesireGraph` until the axis was named, which would now collide with `ag:DesireGraph` meaning the opposite thing.

A class rather than one graph, because a constraint may have more than one source and a reader must not have to know how many: `agent.genesis` resolves a rule's write target from this term, and `store.query` merges every instance into the default graph like any other public knowledge.""" .

<http://example.org/agora/graph/desire> a :RegionGraph ; ag:arrivedBy ag:Derived ;
    rdfs:label "deduced regions" ;
    rdfs:comment "The one instance today: what `rules.ru` computed from the ranges the world states. Cleared and recomputed on every start, because it is a function of the ratified files rather than an accumulation — a plant whose range is amended must not leave an agent holding the old region. The IRI still reads `graph/desire`, kept until a migration makes renaming free; the TYPE carries the truth." .

